YATAP. shimb wiz-orc-fem-cha

I don't know if anyone reads these but decided to write one anyway...
It seems that my game won the best behaved prize in the tournament. 9
conducts - I know that that is easy compared to some really crazy
conduct games but it was something I hadn't done before. Cbus and Tapin
had 8 conducts so I had to do 9. :)

Decided to try a foodless, weaponless, genoless, polyitemless,
polyselfless, wishless game. The obvious choice would have been a monk
but since I had already ascended a monk in the tournament I decided to
play an orcish wizard. Orcish because they start with poison resistance
(no YAADs involving poison). With wizards it's easy to roll several
characters until you start with a ring of slow digestion but I didn't
do that. But I knew I had to find the ring pretty quickly or else die
pretty quickly. And then I found three rings in the first two levels.
Hmm... I started to search for a sink. DL6 had a sink. First ring cold
resistance. Second ring gets regurgitated. I couldn't believe my luck.

My intelligence was 16. That meant no hungerless spell casting. I found
a potion of gain ability and after blessing it quaffed it. I was kind
of horrified to learn that 16 is the maximum intelligence for orcs.
That meant I had to find a helm of brilliance to cast spells. Well,
went to sokoban first and it was the bag of holding one. Left straight
away 'cause I wanted reflection and the giant mimics would have been
too hard to kill. At this point my character was killing things with
her fists and her two large cats were of great assistance. Went to the
mines to collect some daggers (yeah, a true "weaponless" game).

I had started with a potion of polymorph (so handy, no need to worry
about losing poly-itemless accidentally) and when I found a second one
I decided to polymorph my cats. First cat turned into a horse (lame)
called Beast and the second one became a vrock (much better) called
Beauty. Beauty killed all the shopkeepers (sorry Izchak, I forgot to
lock your door) and the mine town priest. Went to get the luckstone and
there Beauty got scared and was no longer tame so I left her there.
Converted the mine town altar and was determined to get crowned (I had
had some scary moments with monsters + wands of sleep). Telepathy would
have been nice too but unfortunately Anhur didn't grant me that (one
more conduct: no telepathy at all during the whole game! :). Finally I
got crowned. I had been hitting n50. n50. n50. repeatedly to get some
monsters. Killed them with daggers.

DL17 had an armour store. And there was a helm of brilliance! (I used
the naming trick to identify it.) I had been saving a scroll of enchant
armour for this and I enchanted it to +3. At this point I had 7 +6
daggers, AC was -8 and the only useful spells were force bolt,
identify, finger of death and drain life. Needed reflection and magic
missile. Ludios had 3 gray dragons (checked it with b!oDetectMonsters).
Castle had the worst dragons: blue and black. Black could have
disintegrated my character and the blue could have exploded my ring of
slow digestion (didn't have a spare one).

Went back up and did the quest. I took some pictures of Dork One and
threw daggers at him. He summoned some nasties, I have never seen that
happen before. On the way back to the castle an Aleax dropped a shield
of reflection! I used that shield the rest of the game because there
weren't any other reflective thingies anywhere. The wand of wishing was
(0:3). D'oh! So tempting... In the Valley of the Dead I found
spellbooks of magic missile and mapping. Great!

I mapped Gehennom and when I got to the bottom of it I started to feel
worried. I had been hoping I would find the missing items there but no,
the only useful item I found was a magic lamp. AC was -10 and that was
worrying me the most. There had been 2 scrolls of enchant armour in the
game so far (one of those I started with), no magic markers, no bones
files, no free action, no conflict, no speed boots, one scroll of gold
detection. (I was wearing black dragon scales so the lack of enchant
armour scrolls was really annoying me.) I was also hoping for a ring of
levitation since my only source of levitation was a -2 pair of
levitation boots. Okay, I had 4 amulets of life saving, three pairs of
jumping boots and a bag of holding so it wasn't all bad.

A master lich started to summon stuff when I was in the Wizard's Tower.
It started to annoy me so I #invoked the Eye and went to do Sokoban.
And what do you know! There were two scrolls of enchant armour in the
Sokoban Zoo. What a relief! Made me a black dragon scale mail and
enchanted the helm of brilliance to +5. Now I had an ascendable AC of
-19. At this point I also got my strength to 18. :)

After that the game went smoothly. Teleporting/summoning/cursing liches
were an annoyance, the mysterious force was being a bitch (hey, my
character is chaotic, not lawful) and had to kill Rodney 10 times but
everything was so easy with the spell of magic missile (though the 156
Pw I had didn't last very long). The planes were easier than I expected
(only had that one scroll of gold detection): on earth just stumbled to
the portal, on air a yellow light showed me the way to go, used the
scroll on fire and on water just searched wielding the amulet. Astral
was _easy_ jumping like a rabbit, the riders didn't even touch my
character. Of course I had the worst luck and the last altar was the
chaotic altar. Didn't have to resort to the cursed -5 (!) helm of
opposite alignment I had found.

Some thoughts: foodless is easy with a ring of slow digestion. Only had
to pray twice for food after finding the ring. But I wasn't wearing any
other rings or amulets during the game so that may have helped. I am
very surprised to learn the true power of that ring. Not hitting with a
weapon was annoying and carrying Magicbane but not wielding it felt so
stupid 'cause everything was getting cursed, even the Magicbane itself.
I engraved with it not knowing it was cursed so I ascended with cursed
-3 Magicbane. :) Wishless was annoying but in the end I realised you
don't need a "perfect Ascension Kit (TM)". Most of the time you can get
away with what you've got. Of course I was sooooo lucky that things
didn't go badly wrong. Anyway it feels kind of wrong to win the best
behaved game with such an easy game. ;P

Thanks for organising such a fun tournament! And congratulations to all
the winners out there!

